# Source Strategy — {{TITLE}}

## Selection order

Prefer sources in this order, adapting to the field:

1. official specifications, syllabi, standards, documentation, or primary works;
2. peer-reviewed or institutionally maintained references;
3. authoritative textbooks or recognized practitioner material;
4. secondary explanations used to clarify, not define, the scope.

For information that changes, verify current status and record the access date or version. Do not invent a citation to fill the table.

Record verified candidates and pinned versions in [[resources/source-lock.csv|the source lock]]. Leave it header-only until a source is actually checked; never invent a version or access date.

