Use the same status vocabulary here and in `source-lock.csv`: `provisional` for an unverified candidate, `current` for a verified source in use, `superseded` for a retained replacement history, or `unavailable` when it cannot be checked or used.

## Source lock checklist

- [ ] The course scope is tied to at least one verified authoritative source.
- [ ] Volatile sources include a version or access date.
- [ ] Each major module identifies its governing source.
- [ ] Conflicts between sources are recorded rather than silently resolved.
- [ ] Paywalled, inaccessible, unsafe, or unauthorized resources have alternatives.

## Research notes

Keep summaries separate from quotations. Link each factual correction to the source that supports it.
